### Service 1: Social Media

**Headline:**
Your customers check your Instagram before they call you.

**Body copy:**

That is just how it works now. A homeowner needs a roofer. They Google your company. Check the reviews. Then they look at your Instagram or Facebook. If the page is dead, they move on.

You do great work. The before and after photos alone would get attention. But you are on a job site all day. Posting does not happen. So the page stays dead and the other guy gets the call.

I plan the content, make the graphics, edit the videos, schedule the posts, and send you a report every month. You do not have to think about it.

**What this covers:**
Content planning, graphic design, short-form video, scheduling, posting, profile setup, monthly reports.

---

### Service 2: Websites

**Headline:**
Pull up your website on your phone. What do you see?

**Body copy:**

If it takes more than 3 seconds to load, you have already lost someone. If the phone number is hard to find, they are calling the next guy. If it looks like it was built 10 years ago, that is what they think about your business.

Most of the roofing websites I see have the same problem. They were set up once, never touched again, and now they are doing more harm than good.

I build sites that load fast, work on every phone, and make it obvious what you do and how to reach you. Nothing fancy. Just a site that does its job.

**What this covers:**
Website design and build, works on all devices, fast loading, contact forms, service pages, project gallery.

---

### Service 3: Operations and Systems

**Headline:**
How many hours do you spend catching up after work every night?

**Body copy:**

Returning missed calls. Following up on estimates from last week. Figuring out tomorrow's schedule. Texting your crew about changes. All of this happens after 5pm because there is no time during the day.

If your process is text messages, memory, and maybe a notebook, stuff is going to slip. Estimates go cold. Callbacks pile up. A customer who waited two days for a follow-up already called someone else.

I build systems that keep track of everything so you do not have to hold it all in your head. Nothing complicated. Just enough structure that things stop falling through.

**What this covers:**
SOPs, workflow setup, task tracking, CRM setup (GoHighLevel, HubSpot, Notion), process documentation, follow-up systems.

---

### Service 4: Custom Tools

**Headline:**
The software you bought is collecting dust. I know.

**Body copy:**

You signed up for Monday. Or Asana. Or whatever someone recommended. Used it for two weeks. It was confusing, nobody on the team liked it, and now everything is back in group texts and spreadsheets.

The problem is not that you need software. The problem is that generic software does not fit how your business actually runs.

I build tools that do. A client portal where your customers approve work with a swipe instead of navigating a confusing dashboard. Reports that generate themselves instead of eating your Sunday afternoon. One screen that shows you everything instead of five tabs and three apps.

I already built one. It replaced Monday.com for a team. It is live right now.

**What this covers:**
Custom web tools, client portals, approval workflows, automated reporting, built with React and Supabase.

